; The Melange mirror of the production closure.
;
; Dune cannot make a library's `modes` conditional: `enabled_if` on a library
; needs (lang dune 3.15) — which we now use — but two stanzas sharing a library
; name in one dune file crash dune with an internal error. Two stanzas sharing a
; name in *different directories*, made mutually exclusive by enabled_if, work.
; So each library appears twice: once under lib/ with (modes byte native), and
; once here with (modes byte native melange), copy_files'ing the very same
; sources so there is exactly one copy of the code.
;
; Why gate it at all: declaring melange mode on a library puts melc rules into
; @all whether or not anything emits JavaScript, so an ungated declaration would
; make `dune build @all` require melc on every CI leg — including the OCaml 5.x
; legs, where Melange 5.1.0-414 (ocaml >= 4.14 & < 4.15) cannot be installed.
;
; ASM_MELANGE is set explicitly by both CI jobs, never left to a default.

(vendored_dirs vendor)
